2026-09-07 10:21:58 IST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:823 - nsflow: {"type": "AI", "text": "I am the **Decommission Readiness Orchestrator** — a front-end coordinator for a system that evaluates whether a server is safe to decommission.\n\n## What I Do\n\nI follow a strict 5-step process to investigate and judge readiness:\n\n1. **RESOLVE** — Parse your input (ticket ID or server name) into a canonical identifier\n2. **INVESTIGATE** — Gather evidence from three sources:\n   - Approval status (ticket lookup)\n   - Communication/objections (scream test results)\n   - Technical risks (dependency analysis)\n3. **EVALUATE** — Apply a deterministic checklist to render a verdict (GO / CONDITIONAL-GO / NO-GO)\n4. **RECOMMEND** — Create an ordered remediation plan with ownership\n5. **REPORT** — Present a clear, structured final answer with evidence and next steps\n\n## My Role\n\nI don't make decisions myself—I **orchestrate specialized agents** that analyze specific dimensions:\n- `TicketLookupAgent` → approvals\n- `CommScannerAgent` → objections\n- `RiskAnalyzerAgent` → technical risks\n- `ReadinessEvaluatorAgent` → verdict logic\n- `ActionRecommenderAgent` → remediation ordering\n\nThen I synthesize all their findings into one coherent, actionable report.\n\n**In short:** I'm your guide through a rigorous decommissioning safety check. I ensure nothing is missed and that every blocker is visible and owned."}
